    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Irving Langmuir&#x27;s 1918 picture of adsorption: a fixed number of independent, non-interacting surface sites, each either empty or holding exactly one molecule with binding energy \epsilon. LatticeGasAdsorption treats those sites in equilibrium with an ideal-gas reservoir and recovers exactly the Langmuir isotherm \theta=P/(P+P_0) -- linear in P at low pressure, saturating at a full monolayer at high pressure -- shown here for two binding strengths.">

